# Excludes test files from the community-ruleset pass (both CI and the local
# pre-push hook use this automatically -- Semgrep reads .semgrepignore the
# same way git reads .gitignore). Generic security rules regularly false-
# positive on test assertions that deliberately reference dangerous-looking
# patterns to verify they're handled safely -- e.g.
# supabase/functions/_shared/email-template.test.ts asserts that generated
# HTML does NOT contain "<script>", which p/security-audit's XSS rule reads
# as "message is used with a <script> tag" with no way to tell it's an
# assertion, not a render. Confirmed via a real CI run (2026-09-12) blocking
# on exactly this.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
